REQ-PB-075 | Implement Template 14 Benefits Register as a native register | Users record benefits with Type (Revenue | Cost | CX | ...), Value (SAR) and Realized amounts, evidence source and Status R/A/G; IDs B01, B02... |ACC A10: T14 persists all 10 columns; realized value awaiting Finance validation is labelled pending and excluded from validated totals

REQ-PB-058 | Prevent double counting: each benefit has a unique owner, baseline, formula and financial-statement or non-financial KPI link | System rejects a benefit without a single owner, baseline, formula and a financial statement line or agreed non-financial KPI; initiatives link to canonical benefits via allocations, parent/child relationships and shared-benefit groups; portfolio totals sum canonical benefits, not links, so a shared benefit rolls up once |ACC A10: a benefit with two owners is rejected; a 10 million SAR benefit shared by two initiatives appears once (10 million SAR) in the portfolio total

REQ-PB-015 | Model the six stage gates G1-G6 as explicit approval records with decision question and evidence required | Owner assembles evidence, submits the gate; approver records decision against the evidence snapshot; gates are never inferred from task completion |ACC A08: submission with missing mandatory evidence is rejected; approval by a non-approver returns 403; approval of a stale submission version is rejected

REQ-PB-021 | G6 Sustain: require benefits evidence, ownership transfer, controls and continuous improvement backlog as gate evidence | G6 checklist links validated benefit evidence, accepted BAU handover, controls and the CI backlog |ACC A08;A11: G6 submission without an accepted BAU handover is rejected listing 'Ownership transfer'

REQ-PB-012 | Seed the six minimum governance roles with their source accountabilities and assign them per transformation | Admin seeds roles; Transformation Lead/Office assign named people to roles per transformation; accountability text shown on the role assignment |ACC A12: a user assigned Workstream Lead on transformation X cannot read transformation Y; role accountability text matches B0018

REQ-S03-003 | Keep initiative delivery, business adoption, validated value and transformation closure as separate statuses | Each status has its own state machine and owner; none is derived from another; views show all four side by side |ACC A11: setting delivery to Complete leaves adoption, validated value and closure unchanged; the API rejects a closure request while validated value is pending unless a transition decision exists

REQ-S08-001 | Track planned, forecast, measured, submitted-for-validation, validated, rejected and sustained benefit values separately | Each benefit keeps separate value series per state; aggregations never combine states |ACC A10: a forecast amount never appears in the validated total; a rejected measurement is retained and shown as rejected

REQ-S08-013 | Reject allocations over 100% and show any share below 100% as unallocated | The server sums allocations per benefit; above 100% is rejected; below 100% shows the remaining share as unallocated |ACC A10: allocations 60% + 50% are rejected; 60% + 30% saves and shows 10% unallocated

REQ-S10-015 | Support sequential or parallel approval rules | Approval routes are configured per procedure or record type |ACC A06;A08: in a sequential route step 2 is not notified until step 1 approves; in a parallel route both are notified at once

REQ-S04-008 | Run the Realize phase procedure and G6 Sustain decision | Measure and validate benefits; correct gaps; transfer ownership and controls; establish sustained monitoring and improvement; submit G6 with the decision 'value is embedded in BAU' |ACC A02;A11: G6 submission without an accepted BAU handover is rejected; product G6 approval changes no engineering DG record
